From 58e578967f6ed75f7581ee54ad85b454cdcd6c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:58:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] HIP/RDNA GDN: DPP segment reductions, state staged as
 16-byte rows through LDS, next token's kv dot product fused into the output
 pass (GGML_HIP_GDN_FAST=0: plain kernel)

Same element-to-lane mapping, same per-lane summation order and the same xor butterfly, so the results are meant to be
bit-identical to the plain kernel:
- warp_reduce_sum (ds_bpermute through LDS, 15 per lag kernel) -> warp_reduce_sum_dpp (DPP row_xmask);
- state read/written as global_load/store_b128 of the warp's 4 contiguous columns, redistributed through 8.5 KB
  LDS per block (rows padded by 8 floats, conflict-free lane reads) instead of 16 scattered dword loads per lane;
- scalar gate: kv[t+1] = S'k[t+1] is summed in the same pass as attn[t] = S'q[t] after the update of token t, both
  butterflies overlap; token t+1's q/k loads and l2 norms are issued before token t's update.
ISA (S_v=128, lag, l2): 0 ds_bpermute (was 15), 24 DPP adds, 4 b128 loads + 8 b128 stores, 119 VGPRs (was 84), no spills.

UNMEASURED (no GPU access at commit time): bitwise check (greedy md5, test-backend-ops GATED_DELTA_NET) and
rocprofv3 timing pending, see QWEN5-ROUND5.md.
